  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1216 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nA strong upper level high will spin over the Central Rockies and \nCentral Plains through mid week then shift west late week into this \nweekend. As for the short range forecast, expect mostly clear skies \nwith periods of high clouds. Dry conditions are expected with winds \nfrom a southerly direction. Highs through Monday will reach around \n100 degrees to low 100s with lows tonight and tomorrow night in the \n70s. The main concern will be the heat indices that are expected to \nreach at or above 105 degrees. A heat advisory as been issued to \naccount for this. The NBM has the highest probability of heat \nindices exceeding 110 degrees will be across south central \nKansas each afternoon. \n\nMid range models show increasing chances of thunderstorms Monday \nnight through Thursday night as weak disturbances move through the \narea. The best chance of precipitation currently look to be across \nfar western Kansas and northern Kansas. Otherwise expect an increase \nin cloud cover. Highs look to reach into the 90s to low 100s with \nlows in the upper 60s to upper 70s.",
